AI video tools do not sell clips. They sell credits, and each model spends a different number of credits per second, per resolution and per feature. That makes the headline monthly price a poor guide to what a finished video costs. This guide compares three well-known tools, Runway, Google Flow (which runs Google's Veo models) and Kling, using what each vendor publishes on its own pricing and help pages. It does not judge video quality, because we have not run these tools side by side. Prices and credit costs change often, so check the live pages before you subscribe. A note on sourcing: Kling's pages, Runway's pricing page and Runway's plan-switch article could not be opened directly when this was written, so figures for them come from excerpts of the vendors' own pages shown in search results. Confirm those on the live pages before you pay.

One note for readers using older guides: OpenAI's own Sora pages now carry a notice that the Sora product is no longer available as of April 26, 2026, so it is left out here.

## How each one charges

| | Runway | Google Flow (Veo) | Kling |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Free option | 125 one-time credits, with a watermark | 50 credits per day, with or without a subscription | Basic plan, no monthly credits |
| Entry paid | Standard: $12 per month billed annually ($15 monthly), 625 credits | Google AI Plus: $7.99, 200 credits a month | Standard: $6.99 first month, then $8.80, 660 credits |
| Middle | Pro: $28 annual ($35 monthly), 2,250 credits | Google AI Pro: $19.99, 1,000 credits a month | Pro: $25.99 first month, then $32.56, 3,000 credits |
| Heavy | Max: $76 annual ($95 monthly), 9,500 credits | Google AI Ultra: $99.99 (10,000 credits); a higher Ultra tier with 25,000 credits is listed at $199.99 on Google's Flow page | Higher tiers vary by page version (see below) |

![Horizontal bar chart of the approximate cost of one AI video generation, from about 20 cents for Veo 3.1 Lite on Google AI Pro to 1 dollar 15 for a Runway Gen-4.5 five second clip on the Standard plan](/images/site1/ai-video-generators-pricing-chart.svg)
*Chart created by Stackbrook from Runway's and Google's published credit and plan pages.*

## Runway

Runway's pricing page lists a Free plan with 125 one-time credits, then Standard, Pro and Max. Its help center says Free videos carry a Runway watermark, and that you need Standard or above to generate without one. Credits cannot be bought on Free.

On Standard and Pro, monthly credits reset on your billing date and do not carry over, while Max rolls over up to one month of unused credits. Purchased extra credits never expire, with a minimum purchase of 1,000 credits. Runway's help center says Pro and higher include access to all models and 4K video upscaling.

Runway lists Gen-4.5 at 12 credits per second of video, so a 5-second clip costs 60 credits and Standard's 625 credits cover about 52 seconds. Runway's "Unlimited plan is switching to Max" help article says the Unlimited plan is being replaced by Max, with existing Unlimited subscribers moving on November 30, 2026.

## Google Flow and Veo

Google's Flow tool is paid for with Flow credits attached to Google AI plans. Without a subscription you get 50 credits per day. Google's Flow page lists AI Plus at $7.99 with 200 extra monthly credits, AI Pro at $19.99 with 1,000, and AI Ultra at $99.99 with 10,000, plus a higher Ultra tier at $199.99 with 25,000. Google's plans page also shows other billing options, so confirm the price you would actually pay. Google's credit page says unused monthly credits do not roll over and that costs and limits can change.

Credit costs per generation, from Google's help page: Veo 3.1 Lite costs 10 credits (5 for Ultra subscribers) for 4, 6 or 8-second 720p videos, Veo 3.1 Fast costs 20 (10 for Ultra), and Veo 3.1 Quality costs 100 for an 8-second video. Google's credits page also says Veo 3.1 Fast and Quality are scheduled to retire on December 5, 2026, so we leave them out of the cost comparison below. Google also notes that without a subscription you may be unable to generate videos during peak hours. Google AI plans bundle other items, such as Gemini features and cloud storage, so the plan price is not all for video.

## Kling

Kling's membership page lists a free Basic plan with no monthly credits, then Standard at $6.99 for the first month and $8.80 after, and Pro at $25.99 for the first month and $32.56 after. Standard includes 660 credits a month and Pro 3,000. The page says generated content on paid plans is for commercial use and on Basic is not, so read Kling's terms before using clips commercially.

Kling's credits policy says subscription credits are valid for one month and purchased credits for two years, at a standard rate of $1 for 66 credits. The pages we found disagree about the higher tiers, listing Premier and Ultra plans at different prices and credit counts in different versions, so we do not compare those here.

## What a generation costs, roughly

Using each vendor's list price and credit costs, and assuming you use every credit in the month (our own arithmetic):

| Option | Rough cost per generation |
| --- | --- |
| Veo 3.1 Lite on Google AI Pro | $0.20 (100 generations from 1,000 credits) |
| Runway Gen-4.5, 5 seconds, Max annual | $0.48 |
| Runway Gen-4.5, 5 seconds, Pro annual | $0.75 |
| Runway Gen-4.5, 5 seconds, Standard annual | $1.15 |

Treat these as ballparks. Veo clips are 4 to 8 seconds and Runway's are 5, models and resolutions differ, and monthly billing on Runway costs more than the annual figures. The Google figure uses the $19.99 monthly price, which also covers other Google AI features, and ignores the free daily credits, which lower the real cost. Kling is left out of the table because its pages describe "standard videos" without a clip length.

## How to choose

- **Trying AI video for free:** Google Flow's daily credits and Runway's 125 one-time credits let you test before paying. Expect a watermark on Runway's free videos.
- **Lowest published price per generation:** Veo 3.1 Lite on Google AI Pro, if its quality and 720p output fit your use.
- **Predictable monthly credits for steady work:** Runway's Pro or Max, remembering that Standard and Pro credits expire monthly.
- **Occasional use on a tight budget:** compare Kling Standard's $8.80 renewal price with Google AI Plus at $7.99 before buying.

Whichever you try, start with one month, since prices, credit costs and model access change often.
